cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EMIL, please cite it and keep the MIT copyright notice of TEMIR."
title: "EMIL: physics-based active ragdoll character core for Godot 4 (C++17, MuJoCo)"
abstract: >-
  EMIL is an open-source active ragdoll: a physics-based character controller that keeps a simulated human body
  standing with joint torques only, takes recovery steps after pushes, and reacts to bullets, hits, trips, drops and
  cars with procedural, physically simulated motion. Written in C++17 on MuJoCo 3.17, with a Godot 4 GDExtension and
  an Android editor app. Very early version.
type: software
authors:
  - name: TEMIR
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
repository-code: "https://github.com/temabot41-dev/emil-ragdoll"
keywords:
